endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
/E (Firstly, fit the supplied brass nipple adaptor to the MAP sensor using thread sealant or thread tape to seal the thread. Next, run the supplied silicone hose from the manifold through a suitable grommet in the firewall to the sensor, ensuring you have fitted the supplied filter inline and are using the supplied hose clamps, keeping the sensor itself secured to a solid mounting point rather than left hanging on the hose. Just as importantly, the sensor should have its own independent tap into the inlet manifold. Sharing a port with the blow-off valve, boost gauge, wastegate feed, or any other consumer introduces pressure fluctuations that the sensor will faithfully report, and the B1 will then chase those fluctuations as if they were real boost changes. A dedicated port costs a few minutes of work and removes the problem entirely.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
