366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (When you select an adjustable zone, the white box highlights the setting and the zone is displayed on the 1st line below settings. In this example is shows as VOLT ZONE 0.0V being the 0.0V zone, which presently, as per the example, is set to offset the duty by 0%. If the text is in red, like the 5 next to the 0 setting, this means it will pull 5% OFF the duty \(reduce the boost\), whereas if the text is in green, it will add the value to the duty \(increase the boost\). 0 is always displayed in white.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6 8 7]
>>
endobj
367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (If you click the knob when you have an adjustable zone highlighted, the blue ball associated with that zone will fade, the VOLT ZONE X.X will also fade, and the ADJ X% will highlight to show you are now in an adjustment mode. If you now turn the knob, the value\(offset\) will adjust the duty associated with that zone. This will be displayed in 3 ways; the 1 row table value, the ADJ X% value, and the ball height. If you are not at the original setting of when you entered that zone e.g. you have adjusted it, the ball will be yellow. If you take it back to the original setting, the ball will change back to faded blue. Please note that the B1 interpolates between zones for a smooth transition.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
