443 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (COMMON: RPM and, less so, speed have common relationships between frequency and RPM/speed. For example, any two six-cylinder engines with a single coil will have the same tach frequency. The LIVE data on the bottom line will give you real-time updates of the displayed RPM/Speed based on your adjustments. If the common frequencies do not give you the correct RPM/Speed, scroll to the COMMON CUSTOM line and click to toggle to CUSTOM. From here, scroll to the frequency line below COMMON CUSTOM and click the knob once. This allows you to adjust the frequency for the RPM displayed to the right of the frequency. If you click the knob again, you can adjust the RPM for the frequency on the left. Clicking the knob again deselects both. So, as an example, if you know that the tach frequency is 45hz at 2200rpm, you would select CUSTOM, scroll to the frequency and click once, turn the knob to adjust the hz to 45hz, click again to select RPM and turn the knob to set to 2200RPM.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
